<div class="hebrew-block">כָּל הָעֲשִׁירוּת שֶׁל כָּל הָעוֹלָם נִמְשָׁךְ רַק מֵהַצַּדִּיק שֶׁרַק הוּא זוֹכֶה לַעֲשִׁירוּת אֲמִתִּי שֶׁעַל יָדוֹ מַשִּיג הִתְבּוֹנְנוּת נִפְלָא, עַל-כֵּן כָּל הָעֲשִׁירוּת שֶׁל כָּל הָעוֹלָם מַגִּיעַ רַק לוֹ לְבַדּוֹ. וְזֶה בְּחִינַת יוֹסֵף הַצַּדִּיק שֶׁזָּכָה לַעֲשִׁירוּת עָצוּם מְאֹד לְכָל הוֹן דְּעָלְמָא, כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב, וַיְלַקֵּט יוֹסֵף אֶת כָּל הַכֶּסֶף וְכוּ'. כִּי יוֹסֵף הַצַּדִּיק זָכָה לְהַשִּיג לְסַפֵּר סִפּוּרֵי מַעֲשִׂיּוֹת הַנַּ"ל שֶׁהֵם בְּחִינַת הַחֲלוֹמוֹת שֶׁסִּפֵּר, שֶׁהֵם בְּחִינַת סִפּוּרֵי מַעֲשִׂיּוֹת מִזֶּה הָעוֹלָם, כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב, וְהִנֵּה אֲנַחְנוּ מְאַלְּמִים אֲלֻמִּים בְּתוֹךְ הַשָּדֶה וְכוּ'. גַּם זָכָה לְסַפֵּר סִפּוּרֵי מַעֲשִׂיּוֹת שֶׁל שָׁנִים קַדְמוֹנִיּוֹת שֶׁזֶּה בְּחִינַת סִפּוּר הַחֲלוֹם הַשֵּׁנִי שֶׁהוּא, וְהִנֵּה הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ וְהַיָּרֵחַ וְאַחַד עָשָׂר כּוֹכָבִים מִשְׁתַּחֲוִים לִי. כִּי כָּל הַזְּמַן שֶׁל כָּל הָאָדָם שֶׁבְּזֶה הָעוֹלָם הַכֹּל נִמְשָׁךְ עַל-יְדֵי הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ וְהַיָּרֵחַ וְהַכּוֹכָבִים שֶׁעַל יָדָם נֶחְשָׁב הַזְּמַן. וּמֵאַחַר שֶׁהוּא זָכָה לְסַפֵּר שֶׁהַשֶּׁמֶשׁ וְהַיָּרֵחַ וְכוּ' מִשְׁתַּחֲוִים אֵלָיו,, זֶהוּ בְּחִינַת שֶׁכָּל הַזְּמַן בָּטֵל אֵלָיו כִּי הוּא לְמַעְלָה מֵהַזְּמַן, כִּי הוּא יוֹדֵעַ סִפּוּרֵי מַעֲשִׂיּוֹת שֶׁל שָׁנִים קַדְמוֹנִיּוֹת שֶׁהֵם בִּבְחִינַת לְמַעְלָה מֵהַזְּמַן. גַּם זָכָה יוֹסֵף לָדַעַת כָּל מַה שֶּׁמְּלֻבָּשׁ וְנֶעְלָם בְּסִפּוּרֵי הַמַּעֲשִׂיּוֹת שֶׁהָעוֹלָם מְסַפְּרִין ]כְּמוֹ שֶׁמּוּבָא בְּהַקְדָּמַת הַסִּפּוּרֵי מַעֲשִׂיּוֹת בְּשֵׁם הַבַּעַל שֵׁם טוֹב זַ"ל שֶׁבְּכָל הַמַּעֲשִׂיּוֹת שֶׁל הָעוֹלָם יֵשׁ בָּהֶם דְּבָרִים גְּנוּזִים, עַיֵּן שָׁם[ וְזֶהוּ בְּחִינַת מַה שֶּׁיָּדַע יוֹסֵף לִפְתֹּר הַחֲלוֹמוֹת שֶׁל פַּרְעֹה וְשֶׁל שַׂר הַמַּשְׁקִים וְהָאוֹפִים. כִּי כָּל הַחֲלוֹמוֹת שֶׁסִּפְּרוּ הֵם בְּחִינַת סִפּוּרֵי מַעֲשִׂיּוֹת, כִּי הַחֲלוֹם הָיָה סִפּוּר מַעֲשֶׂה שֶׁרָאָה שֶׁבַע פָּרוֹת טוֹבוֹת וְשֶׁבַע רָעוֹת וְכוּ' וְכֵן כֻּלָּם. וְיוֹסֵף יָדַע הַסּוֹד כָּל מַה שֶּׁנֶּעְלָם וּמְלֻבָּשׁ בָּהֶם. וְעַל-כֵּן רָאוּ אֵלּוּ הַמַּעֲשִׂיּוֹת בַּחֲלוֹם, כִּי הַמַּעֲשִׂיּוֹת בָּאוּ רַק בִּשְׁבִיל הִתְעוֹרְרוּת הַשֵּׁנָה עַל-כֵּן נִתְגַּלּוּ לָהֶם בַּחֲלוֹם בַּשֵּׁנָה. וְזֶה שֶׁהִתְפַּלֵּא פַּרְעֹה וְאָמַר לְיוֹסֵף כְּשֶׁפָּתַר לוֹ חֲלוֹמוֹ, אַחֲרֵי הוֹדִיעַ אֱלֹקִים אוֹתְךָ אֶת כָּל זֹאת אֵין נָבוֹן וְחָכָם כָּמוֹךָ, אַתָּה תִּהְיֶה עַל בֵּיתִי וְעַל-פִּיךָ יִשַּׁק כָּל עַמִּי וְכוּ'. הַיְנוּ שֶׁאָמַר לוֹ מֵאַחַר שֶׁאַתָּה מַשִּיג כָּל זֶה נִמְצָא שֶׁזָּכִיתָ לְעוֹרֵר מֵהַשֵּׁנָה עַל-יְדֵי סִפּוּרֵי מַעֲשִׂיּוֹת שֶׁעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה זוֹכִין לַעֲשִׁירוּת גָּדוֹל, שֶׁעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה זוֹכִין לְהִתְבּוֹנְנוּת גָּדוֹל כַּנַּ"ל. וְעַל-כֵּן בְּוַדַּאי אֵין נָבוֹן וְחָכָם כָּמוֹךָ וְאַתָּה צָרִיךְ עֲשִׁירוּת מֻפְלָג, עַל-כֵּן אַתָּה תִּהְיֶה עַל בֵּיתִי וְכוּ' וַאֲנִי מוֹסֵר לְךָ כָּל הָעֲשִׁירוּת שֶׁלִּי, כִּי לְךָ מַגִּיעַ כָּל הָעֲשִׁירוּת בִּשְׁבִיל הַהִתְבּוֹנְנוּת, כִּי אֵין נָבוֹן וְחָכָם כָּמוֹךָ וְכַנַּ"ל:</div>

<p class="first"><strong>All the wealth of the entire world</strong> is drawn only from the <em>tzadik</em>, for only he merits true wealth — through which one attains the <em>hisbonenus</em> <span class="added">[contemplation]</span> to contemplate and recognize the greatness of Hashem from all things in the world. For the true wealth is the <em>da'as</em> to see His G-dliness in everything — and this is drawn only through the <em>tzadik</em>.</p>

<p>And therefore, even material wealth — the physical gold and silver of this world — is ultimately drawn through the <em>tzadik</em>. For the physical wealth is a garment and a vessel for the spiritual wealth, which is the <em>da'as</em> and the <em>hisbonenus</em>. And when the spiritual source flows through the <em>tzadik</em>, the physical bounty flows with it. And therefore one must connect oneself to the true <em>tzadik</em> — for through him, both spiritual and material abundance flows to all the world.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <em>nedarim</em> — for through the <em>neder</em>, which draws from the concealed Torah through the <em>tzadik</em>, one draws both spiritual awakening and material abundance into the world. And this is the connection between <em>nedarim</em>, <em>sipuray ma'asiyos</em>, awakening from sleep, <em>pekidos akaros</em>, the redemption from Egypt, and true wealth — they are all one unified concept, all flowing from the concealed Torah, all accomplished through the true <em>tzadik</em>. Blessed be Hashem forever, <em>Amen</em> and <em>Amen</em>.</p>

<hr>

<div class="translator-summary">
<h3>Translator's Summary</h3>

<p>This halacha, based on Likutay Moharan I, Torah 60 ("Pasach Rabbi Shimon"), centers on the concept of awakening from spiritual sleep — and reveals nedarim as the mechanism of that awakening.</p>

<p><strong>Core Teaching:</strong> All things in the world contain dormant, concealed holiness (= concealed Torah). A neder awakens this sleeping holiness, bringing it into revelation — creating new Torah (mitzvah and avayrah) from what was previously neutral. This is precisely the dynamic of "sipuray ma'asiyos" (stories) that awaken those who sleep — for to tell the story of Hashem's deeds is to reveal the concealed holiness within the events of the world.</p>

<p><strong>Key Connections:</strong></p>

<p><strong>Nedarim = Awakening from sleep</strong> — The neder reveals the concealed Torah hidden within things, just as stories awaken the sleeping consciousness.</p>

<p><strong>Chanah's vow</strong> — She vowed a neder when praying for a child, because nedarim (awakening) lead to pekidos akaros (visitation of the barren). Barrenness = dormancy; the neder awakens the dormant flow of life.</p>

<p><strong>Pesach = Peh Sach</strong> — The mouth that tells/speaks — the sipuray ma'asiyos of the Exodus that awaken Israel from the sleep of exile. "Whoever elaborates in telling the Exodus is praiseworthy" — for more telling = more awakening = greater redemption.</p>

<p><strong>Zahav (Gold) = Binah = Concealed Torah = Nedarim</strong> — "Not with silver shall you be redeemed" but with gold — redemption comes through the concealed Torah (Binah), not the revealed. This is also the root of true wealth: da'as/awareness, drawn through the tzadik.</p>

<p><strong>The Tzadik as Source:</strong> All wealth — spiritual and material — flows through the tzadik who connects the concealed Torah to revelation. Nedarim, stories, awakening, fertility, redemption, and wealth are all one concept flowing through this single channel.</p>

